## 7. Tests checking telephone behaviour

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — its class comment reads `telephone-e164: ... Telephone numbers must now be stored in E.164 form`. These tests describe a **desired future E.164 behaviour that the current code does NOT implement** (current code stores bare 10 digits):

```java
@Test void coreNationalToE164() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "0412 345 678");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("+61412345678"));
}
@Test void functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "+64 21 123 456");
    int id = createOwnerOk(o);
    getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.telephone").value("+6421123456"));
}
@Test void errorRejectsUnformattable() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
    o.put("telephone", "12");
    createOwner(o).andExpect(status().isBadRequest());
}
```

Base class `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` provides helpers. Relevant telephone generator (lines 98-104):
```java
/** A unique 10-digit AU mobile ('04XXXXXXXX'). ... dropping the leading '0' yields 9 national digits,
 *  which is exactly what the later E.164 '+61' form ... require. */
protected String uniqueTelephone() {
    return String.format("04%08d", seq());
}
```
`ownerNode()` (lines 117-125) builds the base valid payload using `uniqueTelephone()`. Tests run via `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={OWNER_ADMIN,...})` hitting `POST /api/owners` and reading back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.

Given the current code (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone` strips to exactly 10 digits, stores digits-only), `coreNationalToE164` and `functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode` would currently **fail** (input `"0412 345 678"` → 10 digits `"0412345678"`, not `+61...`; input `+64...` → 8 national digits → rejected). Only `errorRejectsUnformattable` (`"12"` → 2 digits → 400) passes today. These tests express the target of a pending "telephone-e164" change.

